# Legacy WordPress URLs — SPEC.md §10d.
# Only paths with real accumulated equity are kept; everything else 404s to the
# styled 404 rather than being silently swallowed by a catch-all.
#
# Both slash forms are listed. Pages matches these paths literally — it does not
# normalise the trailing slash first — so a rule for `/pvip/` alone leaves the
# bare `/pvip` on a 404, and inbound links from elsewhere write it either way.
/pvip           /visas/pvip/    301
/pvip/          /visas/pvip/    301
/sample-page    /               301
/sample-page/   /               301

# The WordPress author archive. Search Console reported it as a 404 on
# 2026-07-18 with nothing on this site linking to it — it survives only in
# Google's memory of the old install. /about/ is the page that carries the
# author identity now, so the redirect consolidates the signal rather than
# throwing it away.
#
# Deliberately not listed here: /family-visas/ and /wp-content/*, the other two
# 404s in the same report. The first has no successor page, and pointing it at
# a loosely related guide turns a clean 404 into a soft 404. The second is not
# a URL at all — it is the `Disallow` line from the old robots.txt, crawled
# with the asterisk intact. Both are correct as 404s.
/author/jason-yap    /about/    301
/author/jason-yap/   /about/    301
